    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-21T17:52:24+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T17:52:24+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T07:22:24Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T07:22:24Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure and cold front about the west, will move over the remainder of South Australia on Sunday. Another cold front clips the southeast on Monday, followed by a high pressure system, which will then move across southern parts of the state on Tuesday. A trough of low pressure approaches the western border on Wednesday whilst a cold font moves over waters to the south.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-21T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Streaky Bay, most likely later tonight. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm later this evening. Winds north to northwesterly 35 to 50 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h in the evening then tending south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late evening.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers east of Ceduna in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Ceduna in the morning and early afternoon. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming light before dawn then becoming west to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 28 to 33.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 5:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 12 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h increasing to 20 to 30 km/h in the middle of the day then tending south to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 13 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then tending southeast to southwesterly during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower west of Nullarbor in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Ceduna in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then turning south to southeasterly during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 16 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
